# Run requests in order in an HTTP client that retains response cookies (e.g. IntelliJ HTTP Client).
# Configure baseUrl, ownerEmail, ownerPassword, newUserEmail, newUserPassword and replacementPassword
# in your private HTTP client environment; never commit real credentials.
# baseUrl can be http://localhost:8080 for the local profile; production requires HTTPS.

### 1. Start a session and collect the CSRF token
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/csrf

> {% client.global.set("csrf", response.body.token); %}

### 2. Log in; the client must retain the rotated SESSION cookie
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{csrf}}

{"email":"{{ownerEmail}}","password":"{{ownerPassword}}"}

### 3. Fetch a fresh token after successful login
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/csrf

> {% client.global.set("csrf", response.body.token); %}

### 4. Read your own identity
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/me

### 5. Read the contract (OWNER only)
GET {{baseUrl}}/openapi.yaml

### 6. Create a technician (OWNER only)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{csrf}}

{"email":"{{newUserEmail}}","password":"{{newUserPassword}}","role":"TECHNICIAN"}

> {% client.global.set("userId", response.body.id); client.global.set("version", response.body.version); %}

### 7. List accounts (OWNER only)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users?page=0&size=20&sort=employeeNumber&direction=asc

### 8. List active technicians (OWNER or OFFICE; no email addresses)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users/technicians?page=0&size=20

### 9. Change role with the current version
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users/{{userId}}
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{csrf}}

{"role":"OFFICE","version":{{version}}}

> {% client.global.set("version", response.body.version); %}

### 10. Change password; this revokes the target account's sessions
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users/{{userId}}/password
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{csrf}}

{"password":"{{replacementPassword}}","version":{{version}}}

### 11. Fetch the current version after a mutation with no response body
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users/{{userId}}

> {% client.global.set("version", response.body.version); %}

### 12. Deactivate; email remains reserved
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users/{{userId}}/deactivate
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{csrf}}

{"version":{{version}}}

### 13. Logout requires CSRF too
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/logout
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{csrf}}
